{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and the endpoint returned 200.\n\n**Root cause:** The `rate` deployment had `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=20` with `RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY=256`. That limit was too low for the load `search` puts on it. Requests queued and returned `ResourceExhausted`, and `search` (750 ms timeout, 3 attempts) then failed with `DeadlineExceeded`.\n\n**Fix:** Raised `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT` from 20 to 1000 on the `rate` deployment in `hotel-reservation`. The rollout completed successfully.\n\n**Verification:** After the rollout, `search` logged no downstream warnings over the last 30 seconds, and `rate` showed no errors. All pods are Running.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- I could not read the `rate` service source, so the new limit of 1000 is an estimate rather than a value derived from the code.\n- The `RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY=256` setting was left unchanged.\n- I did not check end-to-end latency through the frontend or traces, only the `search` and `rate` logs."}}
